{"id": "840dcb94-f126-4362-a443-90d68657e308", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll pull together the full picture on these three resources — I need to map every layer (data, compute, network, shared dependencies) in `eu-central-1` before I can tell you which DR strategy fits and where the gaps are. Let me gather that now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_UQ3vGUmv3ZHCuYhi7rHk1Y", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"deep_research": true, "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run a read-only resilience/DR data-gathering pass on a workload named by these three resources in eu-central-1, AWS account 012345678901_1: dr-demo-mysql, dr-demo-valkey, dr-demo-players. Identify what dr-demo-players actually is (EC2/ASG, ECS service, EKS, Lambda, or other compute) since its type is unknown — use ec2:DescribeInstances, autoscaling:DescribeAutoScalingGroups, ecs:ListClusters/DescribeServices, lambda:ListFunctions, eks:ListClusters filtered by name/tag 'dr-demo' to find it. Then map the full workload: resources connected to these three by configuration (same CloudFormation stack if any, security groups, VPC, load balancer in front, secrets/KMS keys used, container images/AMIs, IaC).",
  "context": "User is scoping a Region-failure DR plan for an application backend. Business targets given: customer and purchase data need RPO 15 minutes and RTO 1 hour if eu-central-1 fails. The Valkey cache (dr-demo-valkey) is confirmed rebuildable from the database (dr-demo-mysql) — do not treat it as a source of truth, but check whether it can be recreated in a recovery Region and whether the app tolerates an empty/cold cache. dr-demo-mysql is presumed to hold the customer/purchase data (confirm this). No recovery Region has been chosen yet by the user.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql (RDS/Aurora, type unconfirmed)", "dr-demo-valkey (ElastiCache Valkey)", "dr-demo-players (type unknown, locate it)", "eu-central-1", "account 012345678901_1"],
  "timeframe": "current state, not time-bounded",
  "criteria": "For each resource return ONE ROW in this exact format: layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy (AZs, nodes, tasks) | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies, images or IaC outside the Region | point-in-time recovery | replication | what could not be read. Specifically gather: (1) dr-demo-mysql: engine, MultiAZ, BackupRetentionPeriod, ReadReplicaDBInstanceIdentifiers, DeletionProtection, StorageEncrypted, any DescribeGlobalClusters/cross-Region read replica, DescribeDBInstanceAutomatedBackups for replicated backups, DescribeDBSnapshots and their Region. (2) dr-demo-valkey: DescribeReplicationGroups for node/replica count, AutomaticFailover, MultiAZ, SnapshotRetentionLimit, GlobalReplicationGroupInfo, node family/size; DescribeSnapshots. (3) dr-demo-players: full config per its type (AZs/subnets used, desired/min capacity, image/AMI source and whether that image exists in candidate recovery Regions, whether it's stateless). (4) Entry/routing: any load balancer, Route 53 records, or API Gateway in front of dr-demo-players — AZs spanned, failover routing configured or not. (5) Shared dependencies: VPC/subnets/NAT gateway topology (single zonal NAT gateway risk), security groups, Secrets Manager secrets and KMS keys used (and whether replicated to another Region), container image/AMI registry location. (6) Any CloudFormation stack or tags linking these three resources together, and any other resources sharing that stack/tag so the workload boundary is accurate. Note every denied or empty call explicitly as not-checked, not as 'no gap'. Do not recommend a strategy or write the final report — just return the data rows and anything structurally notable (e.g., single-AZ compute, no load balancer, backup retention value, whether a cross-Region replica or snapshot copy already exists)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Mapping dr-demo workload resources and DR posture in eu-central-1."}], "created_at": null}

